BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ab1dd5f78be0a8e883e1b857025b15abfbd0879d@pushpin.city
DTSTAMP:20261114T153123Z
DTSTART:20261120T231500Z
DTEND:20261121T011500Z
SUMMARY:The Dambuilders - TWO SHOWS with Special Guests
LOCATION:The Burren\, 247 Elm St\, Somerville\, MA 02144
DESCRIPTION:The Dambuilders' inventive blend of indie rock\, pop\, and elec
 tric violin earned them a devoted following on college radio in the 1990s.
  Originally formed in Honolulu\, the band relocated to Boston in 1990 and 
 went on to release six albums\, including three for Elektra Records\, tour
  extensively throughout North America\, Europe\, and Australia\, and share
  stages with artists including Lush\, Luna\, Jeff Buckley\, Weezer\, Everc
 lear\, and others. Their acclaimed 1994 album Encendedor featured “Shrin
 e\,” named one of MTV’s 100 Greatest Songs of the ’90s\, Lollapalooz
 a edition. The Dambuilders reunited in 2025\, performing their 1989 debut 
 in its entirety\, and returned with “Shrine 2026\,” their first new re
 lease in decades\, accompanied by a new song\, “I Hope We’re Not Too L
 ate.” The new lineup includes original members Dave Derby\, Kevin March\
 , and Eric Masunaga\, along with guitarist Sean Eden (Luna) and violinist 
 Claudia Chopek (Father John Misty\, TV on the Radio).\nhttps://tickets.24h
 ourmusic.com/eventperformances.asp?evt=1911\nFrom Pushpin Boston: https://
 pushpin.city/
URL:https://tickets.24hourmusic.com/eventperformances.asp?evt=1911
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
