SUMMARY:Holiday Concert Benefitting Foster Love
LOCATION:The Burren\, 247 Elm St\, Somerville\, MA 02144
DESCRIPTION:Tonight\, Jamie Dunphy & True North celebrate the release of th
 eir new holiday 7-inch\, A Post-Punk Christmas Card\, featuring the origin
 al single “Give Me Something Good for Christmas.” The band features th
 ree seasoned musicians with a long history in the Boston music scene: Jami
 e Dunphy (The Beige\, Mill City Trio)\, Seth Peterson (Electric Standard\,
  The Gone Boys\, Capital 6) and Tod Salmonson (The Snap Daddies\, Dr. Smig
 ley's Baby). The trio formed in 2018 and have been performing regularly si
 nce at Boston-area venues including the Burren Backroom\, the Midway Cafe\
 , Lilypad Inman and the Square Root. In May 2025\, the band released Stage
  Dive Into Oblivion\, a collection of four singles including The Last Song
 \, 1983\, Everything Must Go\, and Snowfall\, which Stereo Stickman called
  "a gorgeously refreshing classic."\nhttps://tickets.24hourmusic.com/event
 performances.asp?evt=1931\nFrom Pushpin Boston: https://pushpin.city/
URL:https://tickets.24hourmusic.com/eventperformances.asp?evt=1931
END:VEVENT
