SUMMARY:Brian O’Donovan Legacy Series: Rockaway Bound
LOCATION:The Burren\, 247 Elm St\, Somerville\, MA 02144
DESCRIPTION:Rockaway Bound is a new project led by award-winning Irish acco
 rdion player Diarmuid Ó Meachair\, inspired by the vibrant Irish music sc
 ene that flourished on New York’s Rockaway Peninsula during the 1920s an
 d 1930s. Legendary musicians including the McNulty Family\, Peter Conlon\,
  Michael Coleman\, Paddy Killoran and John McKenna performed in Rockaway d
 uring the summer months\, helping shape the distinctive sound of Irish mus
 ic in America’s golden gramophone era. Rockaway Bound aims to capture th
 e spirit\, energy and creativity of this period while bringing its legacy 
 into the present day. The band’s first run of shows will take place in J
 anuary 2027\, Diarmuid will be joined by some of the most exciting young m
 usicians in Irish traditional music: Seamus Noonan (flute)\, Andrew Caden 
 (fiddle)\, Colman Connolly (piano) and Richard Osban (Greek bouzouki).\nht
 tps://tickets.24hourmusic.com/eventperformances.asp?evt=1929\nFrom Pushpin
  Boston: https://pushpin.city/
URL:https://tickets.24hourmusic.com/eventperformances.asp?evt=1929
